    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1074-a1">

                <pb facs="1163" n="1067" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1067"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 120.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cooper to Mr.
                            Sewall.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, H. I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February 25,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received with profound sorrow the
                    information conveyed in your letter of the 25th instant of the calamity to the
                    United States ship <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, and note that Admiral
                    Miller has directed that the colors of his squadron be placed at half mast until
                    further notice.</p>
                <p>In token of the sympathy of this Government for the Government of the United
                    States in the loss of its gallant officers and men, the garrison flag will be
                    placed at half staff during to-morrow the 26th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry E. Cooper</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
